  <section id="provimux" class="pck-section" aria-labelledby="provimux-title">
    <div class="pck-page">
      <div class="pck-band">
        <div>
          <h2 id="provimux-title">Works well with Provimux and pi-provimux</h2>
          <p>
            Through a proxy, one Pi provider serves models of many labs, and a model can come from a subscription login or an API key, whose caches can last differently: a
            Claude login keeps a cache for an hour, a Claude API key for 5 minutes by default. pi-cache-keeper knows no proxy. It asks over Pi's event bus,
            and <a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/pi-provimux">pi-provimux</a> answers for Provimux and CLIProxyAPI with where each model comes from.
          </p>
        </div>
        <p class="pck-links">
          <a class="button primary" href="https://provimux.providers.dev/">Provimux</a>
          <a class="button" href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/pi-provimux">pi-provimux on npm</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

